# render-card demo — sections, subtitle and footer (blueprint theme).
name: your-first-card
title: The anatomy of a card
subtitle: heading, prose, sections, footer
theme: blueprint
description: |
  A card carries a NAME (the frame rules), a title, an optional
  subtitle, the body, an optional footer — and the body may carry
  its own sections. A line starting with #s begins one:

  ## Sections

  Each section keeps its heading while the frame wraps its prose
  to the same inner width as the rest of the card.

  ## Reading modes

  `render-card --plain` prints everything above with no frame
  glyphs at all; `render-card --themes` draws one sample card in
  every registered theme for side-by-side comparison.
footer: render-card --help for the full flag list
